              "newText": "If any proper, undisputed invoice is not paid within thirty days of its due date, Vendor's sole remedy is interest on the overdue amount at the lesser of one percent per month or the maximum rate permitted by Applicable Law, accruing from the due date until payment. Customer shall not be liable for any liquidated damages, penalty, or similar sum."
